WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.322
Equilibrium propagation, or EP,

00:00:04.402 --> 00:00:08.724
is an appealing way to train neural networks
directly on physical substrates like brains or analog chips,

00:00:08.804 --> 00:00:13.127
because it computes gradients using only the
network's own relaxation dynamics.

00:00:13.207 --> 00:00:17.529
But it comes with two strict requirements: the
weights must be perfectly symmetric,

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:21.931
and the nudge that pushes the network toward its
target must be infinitesimally small.

00:00:22.011 --> 00:00:26.333
Both are very hard to satisfy in real physical hardware.

00:00:26.413 --> 00:00:30.736
And crucially,

00:00:30.816 --> 00:00:35.138
whether weight asymmetry actually harms learning
had never been pinned down,

00:00:35.218 --> 00:00:39.540
because in practice its effect gets tangled up with
the error introduced by using a finite nudge.
